# Defect 393, 2026-10-06 (lane b13-c382's measurement, landing panel 195).
# `heroes fmt` cost the square of a literal's length: one `constant` of
# 20,000 elements retired 141 billion instructions, about four times as many
# for each doubling, and `heroes probe` judges nine variants of a file under
# `multi` alone. `print/elements.hero` grew a bracket's elements, and a
# chain's operands, through a record's field, `b.items @ b.items.push(...)`,
# and a field is no plain name, so each push copied every element before it
# (spec § 10 grows in place a plain name alone). They grow in a name of their
# own now and are stored once: 8,000 elements 24.8 billion instructions
# before, 3.6 after, two times for each doubling, and `fmt` writes every
# tracked `.hero` file byte for byte as it did.
#
# No golden form holds a cost, so this case holds the three loops' output:
# `canonical` formats it and finds it unchanged, and `probe` judges its
# variants. An array, a map and a chain whose operators each carry a comment,
# each long enough that a copy per element would have been the whole of the
# work. The sums weigh each element by its place, so an element out of order
# moves them.

